# Two things live here: simulator/ holds the engine, the agent bundle and the
# web app, and train/ holds the pipeline that produces the agent's weights.
# Everything else at the top level -- card CSVs, scratch notebooks, the HF
# staging tree -- stays untracked.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/simulator/
!/train/
!/.github/
!/.github/workflows/
!/.github/workflows/*.yml
!/render.yaml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- inside simulator/
# Card scans: 683 MB of artwork, tracked via Git LFS (see .gitattributes)
# rather than excluded outright, since the GHCR image build needs them.

# Build products. libcg.so is compiled from simulator/ptcg_engine/src by
# build_engine.sh, which also installs it into each agent bundle; keeping a
# binary in git only creates a copy that can go stale against the source.
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The agent's weights are the exception to the blanket rule the training repo
# uses for *.pt: without them simulator/agents/ is a directory that cannot play,
# and at 11 MB they sit far under GitHub's limits.
!simulator/agents/**/*.pt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- inside train/
# Corpora and checkpoints. The parquet corpora (104 MB), the value-head dataset
# and the .pt checkpoints are regenerated by build_corpus.py / make_value_data.py
# and bc_train.py from replays, so the recipe is worth tracking and the output
# is not. The frozen opponents' bc_policy.pt are 10 MB each and fall under the
# same rule -- unlike simulator/agents/, nothing here has to ship ready to play.
/train/**/*.parquet
/train/**/*.npz
/train/**/*.pt

# cg/ is the engine's prebuilt binaries copied in for training runs; the source
# is simulator/ptcg_engine/src. *.so, *.dll and *.dylib above already cover them.

# WSL leaves these behind next to files copied from Windows.
*Zone.Identifier
